{
 "id": "Scene3D",
 "name": "scene-3d",
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Scene3D: a 3D scene from named primitives",
 "prompt": "Show a ring-stacking toy in 3D that I can drag to turn, without working out a camera or any matrices.",
 "level": 3,
 "use_cases": [
  "onboarding"
 ],
 "form_factor": "phone",
 "keywords": [
  "3d",
  "3d scene",
  "3d model",
  "three d",
  "turntable",
  "product view",
  "rotate object",
  "orbit",
  "drag to rotate",
  "spin",
  "exploded view",
  "assembly animation",
  "cube",
  "sphere",
  "cylinder",
  "cone",
  "torus",
  "primitives",
  "wireframe"
 ],
 "teaches": [
  "Name the parts, not the maths: {\"Scene3D\": {\"objects\": [{\"shape\": \"box\", \"size\": [w, h, d], \"at\": [x, y, z], \"color\": \"@colors.primary\"}]}}; units are yours, Y up, Z toward the viewer",
  "The server frames the scene: one camera distance expression of the window's aspect keeps every part in view at every angle the drag can reach, phone to landscape to a 2x2 widget",
  "orbit (default on) is two touchExpressions on touchX() / touchY(); autorotate adds the clock; assemble flies the parts in by step and back out, eased with smooth_step",
  "Mono: every part is a background-filled mesh with its quad edges drawn in onSurface (hidden lines removed), and nothing moves unless dragged",
  "3D support has not landed in androidx yet (coming): this plays in the C++ and TypeScript players"
 ],
 "pitfalls": [
  "The overlay slot is the place for a title: the scene itself always fills the window"
 ],
 "snippets": [
  {
   "pointer": "/root/Scene3D",
   "shows": "3d.scene",
   "note": "the whole call: parts with shape, size, position and theme colour; camera, lights and framing are the server's"
  },
  {
   "pointer": "/root/Scene3D/objects",
   "shows": "3d.mesh",
   "note": "cylinders, tori and a sphere: each a meshPrimitive3D, shared by parts of the same shape and size"
  },
  {
   "pointer": "/root/Scene3D",
   "shows": "input.drag",
   "note": "orbit is on by default: drag left-right to spin, up-down to tilt"
  }
 ],
